Creating a website involves six main stages:
Planning & Strategy: Define the site's purpose, target audience, key features, and structure (sitemap).
Design & UI/UX: Create wireframes and visual mockups to map out layout, color schemes, fonts, and user experience.
Front-End Development: Build the user-facing part of the site using HTML (structure), CSS (styling), and JavaScript (interactivity).
Back-End Development:Set up the server, database, and logic using languages like Python, Node.js, or PHP to handle dynamic data and user management.
Hosting & Domain: Purchase a domain name (web address) and configure hosting to make the site files accessible on the internet.
Testing & Launch:Check for broken links, mobile responsiveness, and browser compatibility, then deploy the site live.
Maintenance & Updates: Regularly update plugins, security patches, and content to keep the site secure and functional.
Analytics & Optimization:Monitor user behavior via tools like Google Analytics and optimize site performance, speed, and conversion rates over time.
